<title>USA: Starbucks added to S&amp;P MidCap 400 Index.</title>
<headline>Starbucks added to S&amp;P MidCap 400 Index.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The financial information services group of Standard &amp; Poor's said on Thursday that it will add Starbucks Corp to the S&amp;P MidCap 400 Index, replacing AST Research Inc.</p>
<p>The replacement will take effect after the close of trading on May 19, Standard &amp; Poor's said in a statement.</p>
<p>It added that the Korean company Samsung Electronics Co is acquiring all of the common shares of AST Research that it does not already own in a friendly cash tender offer that will also expire May 19.</p>
<p>Starbucks, headquartered in Seattle, operates a chain of coffeehouses that sell gourmet coffee, pastries and related products.</p>
</text>
